From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MANET <manet@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: bcm2711-rpi-cm4: limit PCIe to 2.5 GT/s

With the MT7916 M.2 card behind the IO-BASE-A's M-key to A+E adapter, the
5 GT/s link flaps: the root port raises PME/AER/bandwidth-notification
interrupts until IRQ 27 is disabled, and the next MMIO access to the card
raises an asynchronous SError panic. kernel.panic then reboots the board
every one to six minutes. At 2.5 GT/s the same hardware runs cleanly, and
the link still carries several times the radio's traffic.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-cm4.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-cm4.dts
index 233dfe8..9e5b197 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-cm4.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-cm4.dts
@@ -221,6 +221,12 @@
 };
 
 &pcie0 {
+	/* At 5 GT/s the M.2 Wi-Fi link through carrier adapters drops, and the
+	 * next MMIO access raises an asynchronous SError panic. 2.5 GT/s still
+	 * carries several times the radio's traffic.
+	 */
+	max-link-speed = <1>;
+
 	pci@0,0 {
 		device_type = "pci";
 		#address-cells = <3>;
